# Burn & Build Diet preview PDF (program report printout)

When the user asks for **PDF creation, PDF updates, printout layout, or program-report print changes**, work in the **program report preview pipeline** — not the web UI unless they explicitly ask for web.

## PDFKit (locked — do not change)

These documents are **created with PDFKit** (`server/pdf/`, `PDFDocument` via `server/pdf/draw.js`). This is the **only** approved way to build and deliver program-report printouts.

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Edit PDFKit renderer + draw helpers | HTML/CSS print views, browser print, or client-side PDF libs |
| `npm run render:program-report-preview` → commit PDFs → raw GitHub download links | Artifacts panel, blob URLs, or burnandbuilddiet.com unless explicitly asked |

## Pipeline (source of truth)

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| PDF engine | **PDFKit** — `server/pdf/draw.js` (`PDFDocument`) |
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderProgramReportLockedPreview.js` |
| Shared draw helpers | `server/pdf/drawSeminar.js`, `server/pdf/drawFrame.js` |
| Macro signal data | `js/foodPlanPrintout.js` |
| Payload | `js/programReportPrintout.js` + `js/programReportPreviewFixtures.js` |
| Answers page (PDF page 12) | `js/answersConfirmationPrintout.js` |
| Locked copy | `js/programReportCopy.js` |
| Food list gram scaling | `js/stapleServingPrintout.js` — see `.cursor/rules/burn-engine-servings.mdc` |
| Render script | `scripts/render-program-report-preview.mjs` |
| 1982 reference PDF | `docs/archive/kwarner-1982-original.pdf` |

## Mandatory after every PDF change

1. Run **`npm run render:program-report-preview`**
2. Script writes **three sample files**:
   - **Versioned:** `docs/samples/burn-and-build-diet-kristi-N.pdf` (N auto-increments, never overwrite)
   - **Archive:** `docs/samples/burn-and-build-diet-kristi-archive-vN.pdf`
   - **Latest (stable):** `docs/samples/burn-and-build-diet-kristi-latest.pdf` (overwritten each render)
3. **Commit and push to `main`:** versioned PDF, latest PDF, and archive
4. **Give the user the raw download link** (see below)

Optional: copy to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/` when that folder exists — never rely on it for delivery.

## Download delivery (locked — do not change)

The user downloads PDFs to **Mac Downloads** by tapping a **raw GitHub URL**. This is the only delivery method unless they explicitly ask for something else.

### Give the user

Paste **both** raw links after every render (after push to `main`):

- **Versioned:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/<versioned-filename>`
- **Latest:** `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/burn-and-build-diet-kristi-latest.pdf`

State the exact versioned filename (e.g. `burn-and-build-diet-kristi-45.pdf`).

### Never use for delivery

| Wrong | Why |
|-------|-----|
| `github.com/.../blob/...` | Opens GitHub in the browser — does not download |
| Cursor artifacts panel | PDFs have no web preview; download UX is broken on Cursor Web |
| `burnandbuilddiet.com` links | Only when user explicitly asks for a hosted link |
| Telling user to run local commands | They expect a tap-to-download link |

The render script prints `DOWNLOAD` and `DOWNLOAD_LATEST` lines — use those URLs in the response.
